      "writtenOn": "2026-10-13T08:20:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi @praveenbv@ami.com,\n\nI understand the concern. If GPIO and Analog interfaces overlap at the same inventory path, the conflicting add could be lost. Based on my understanding of the current Ventura2 design and the Entity Manager configuration (https://github.com/openbmc/entity-manager/blob/master/configurations/meta/ventura2/ventura2_valve.json) I checked, GPIO and Analog valves use different names and therefore different inventory paths. I don’t expect a valve to change between those types at the same path in this design. \n\nGiven that scope, I’d prefer to keep the current implementation rather than add tracking for both interfaces at one path. \n\nPlease let me know if I’m missing a supported use case that requires such a transition.",
